+## Sites
+
+A request names its site in the `X-Larder-Site` header; without it the site is
+`main`. A site that does not exist is a 400 with code `unknown_site`, on every
+route.
+
+Only the request's site is seen by: batches and their movements, stock on hand
+(in items, `GET /items/:id`, CSV exports and forecasts), cooking, alerts, the
+stock value and waste reports, the ledger export, stock-takes and the locations
+an order is received into. A batch or stock-take of another site answers as if
+it did not exist; a location of another site is `unknown_location`.
+
+Items, suppliers, prices, recipes, dishes and orders are shared. Temperature
+logs and their report cover every site's locations, and `POST /jobs/nightly`
+checks every site whatever the header says.
